I spent the weekend making a tiny website that shows the phase of the moon as an emoji in your browser tab title, and it changes every few hours. It's useless but I love it. Here's the core of the code:

```js
const phases = ['🌑','🌒','🌓','🌔','🌕','🌖','🌗','🌘'];
const synodic = 29.53058867;
const known = new Date('2000-01-06T18:14:00Z');
const days = (Date.now() - known) / 86400000;
const idx = Math.floor(((days % synodic) / synodic) * 8);
document.title = phases[idx];
```

